>>>>> clauses"; I think you mean a prepositional phrase. Neither is an 
>>>>> adjective or 
>>>>> adverb;
>>>>
>>>>
>>>> they are adverbs.
>>>>
>>>
>>> No.
>>>  
>>>
>>>>  those parts of speech, which are classes of single words, don't exist 
>>>>> in Lojban.
>>>>
>>>>
>>>> All SAE languages have adverbs. Lojban is no exception.
>>>>
>>>
>>> Lojban is not an SAE language.
>>>
>>
>> Lojban must optionally work as a SAE language. Otherwise it's alien and 
>> not usable by SAE-speakers.
>>
>
> No, Lojban mustn't do anything. And no, it's not unusable by speakers of 
> SAE languages if it doesn't conform to SAE. Japanese isn't SAE, and yet 
> there are many English-natives who are perfectly capable of speaking it.
>  
>
>>  There is no syntactic difference between "le mlatu cu blabi" and "le 
>>>>> blabi cu mlatu", indicating that "mlatu" and "blabi" belong to the 
>>>>> same part 
>>>>> of speech. 
>>>>>
>>>>
>>>> {le mlatu} is a noun.
>>>>
>>>
>>> *sumti
>>>  
>>>
>>>> {mlatu} is a verb.
>>>>
>>>
>>> *selbri
>>>
>>
>>
>> The more you replace understandable terms to fenki terms the fewer people 
>> are willing to learn Lojban.
>> Of course it's your choice but please don't try ban other terminologies 
>> for the same language.
>>
>
> The more you use incorrect terms the more you will confuse people and 
> cause them to make mistakes based on faulty assumptions. {LO broda} is *
> not* a noun, it is a sumti. The English equivalent of sumti is 
> "argument". {broda} is not a verb, it is a selbri: "relationship word".
>
> It's not a matter of choice, it's not a matter of banning, it's a matter 
> of using an accurate term to describe a part of speech. "noun", "verb", 
> "adjective", "adverb", etc., are not accurate words to describe *any*part of Lojban speech, and it's certainly not crazy to use words that are.
>

co'a xajmi

I've monitored chat logs and I can see many people STILL making mistakes 
even when using this "correct" terminology.
Not counting numerous other people who just stopped reading lojbanic 
grammar because of these strange terms.
It looks like you need to love Lojban before knowing anything about it 
because it's textbooks are terrible.

So I can see no advantages of using alien terminology.



